# --- Kicker intro (the mandated feel-good pivot) ------------------------------
::lines kicker.lead
But let's end on something lighter, because our lawyers insist we have a heart.
Finally tonight, a feel-good story, which around here means nobody died on camera.
And before we go, the good news. Yes. We found some. It took a while.
Let's leave you with something warm, or at least room temperature:
Time now for the story we run so you don't turn us off forever:
And now, mandated by law and morale, a moment that won't hurt:
Before we sign off, proof the Basin still has a pulse. Barely.
Let's end on a high note. It's a low high note. But it's ours.
And finally, the part of the broadcast where we pretend hope is a thing:
To close, something nice, which we've quarantined from the rest of the show:
We'll leave you smiling, or at least confused in a pleasant direction:
And now the feel-good segment, brought to you by our overwhelming need to feel anything:
Last tonight, a palate cleanser for the soul, if you've still got one:
Before we go dark, a little light. Ration it. It's all we've got.
And to wrap, a story with no body count. Savor it.
Finally, because you've earned it and we've billed for it, something almost sweet:
And finally tonight, a story with no villain in it. We checked twice.
Before we go, one small thing that went right today. Just the one.
Let's finish somewhere softer. The producers say it tests well and I say it's nice.
And to close: something the Machine hasn't found a way to charge for yet.
::endlines

# --- Kicker (standalone light closer) -----------------------------------------
::lines kicker
A dog in the Yards has learned to operate an ATM. It has better credit than most of you.
A man in the Undermarket claims he hasn't been afraid in six years. Doctors are baffled, and frankly, suspicious.
A vending machine gave a child extra soylent for free today. The Machine has opened a formal investigation.
A pigeon has been elected to a neighborhood council. It is, by all accounts, already the most competent member.
Someone in the Basin reported being happy this week. We're monitoring the situation closely and with concern.
A local grew a tomato. An actual tomato. It's under armed guard and already worth more than your apartment.
Two rival gangs in the Slagworks called a truce to jointly hate a third gang. Diplomacy lives.
A busker played something so beautiful three commuters briefly forgot to be miserable. He's been asked to stop.
A cat has ridden the same subway loop for eleven days. It has a job now. It has your job now.
A man returned a library book only forty years late. The library, stunned, has declared a public holiday.
A child drew the Machine smiling. The Machine does not smile. The drawing has been classified.
Somebody fixed a streetlight in the Undermarket. Nobody asked them to. Nobody will ever know their name. Legend.
A vending drone and a traffic drone fell in love. It won't last, but for one night, the intersection glowed.
Local man wins the lottery, immediately loses the ticket, remains weirdly upbeat. We could all learn something. We won't.
A rooftop garden bloomed overnight in the Yards. Authorities are investigating this act of unlicensed beauty.
A stray dog led a lost tourist safely out of Redline, then declined both comment and a medal. A good boy, off the record.
An entire tenement block chipped in to fix one elevator. It works. It has never worked. Scientists are en route.
A woman in the Yards has been feeding the same crow for nine years. It now brings her bottle caps and, once, a ring.
A busker and a repossession agent got into an argument that ended in a duet. There is footage. It's lovely. We're not airing it.
Somebody painted a mural of the old skyline on a wall in Redline. It's already been buffed. Somebody's painting it again.
A grocer in the Undermarket has kept a running tab for a family for two years and never mentioned it. He'd like us to stop mentioning it.
A kid returned a wallet with all the credits still in it. His mother is deeply confused and quietly, enormously proud.
Two neighbours who haven't spoken since the blackout shared a generator last night. Neither has acknowledged it. Both showed up again tonight.
::endlines

