We've told you everything we're allowed to and half of what we're not. I'm {anchor}. Good night.
That's the broadcast. Go hug someone, then check the locks. I'm {anchor}.
I'm {anchor}, and on behalf of everyone still standing at Raptor News: courage. You'll need it by breakfast.
Time's up, and so, probably, are we. {anchor} saying good night, Coldwater Basin. Try to be here tomorrow.
That's tonight. Stay scared, stay smart, stay watching. I'm {anchor}, and I mean "watching" literally.
From all of us to whichever of you are left, good night. I'm {anchor}. Ration the hope.
We now return you to your regularly scheduled dread. I'm {anchor}. Thank you for being afraid with us.
That's the news that fit. The rest we're saving for when it's worse. I'm {anchor}. Good night.
I'm {anchor}. Keep your head down and your dial here; it's the safest place in the Basin, statistically, per us.
And that's a wrap on tonight's fury. I'm {anchor}. Go carefully, the city's in a mood.
